    "title": "Heavy rain, severe weather possible by Thursday evening - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Chuck Samples ,\n1 days ago Strong to severe storms and heavy rainfall are still possible areawide after sunset Wednesday. The Storm Prediction Center has a slight-to-enhanced severe weather risk areawide, with the enhanced area along and south of a line from Kingman to Madison to Parsons. Regardless of the risk level, the main concern is heavy rainfall — possibly up to 1.5 inches of rain — along with large hail, wind gusts up to 70 mph and brief, isolated tornadoes. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
    "summary": "15 hours ago Strong to severe storms and heavy rainfall are still possible areawide after sunset Wednesday. The Storm Prediction Center has a slight-to-enhanced severe weather risk areawide, with the enhanced area along and south of a line from Kingman to Madison to Parsons. Regardless of the risk level, the main concern is heavy rainfall — possibly up to 1.5 inches of rain — along with large hail, wind gusts up to 70 mph and brief, isolated tornadoes. Read full article",
